---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import { breadcrumbs, service } from '../data/site.js';
const crumbs = [['Services', '/services'], ['Wildlife management plans', '/wildlife-management-plans']];
const ld = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@graph': [
  service({ name: 'Wildlife management plan', serviceType: 'Wildlife management plan', path: '/wildlife-management-plans',
    description: 'A comprehensive wildlife management plan built from an on-foot assessment: species goals, habitat, food, cover and water work, census, and a practice calendar. For Texas properties, prepared to file for wildlife tax exemption.' }),
  breadcrumbs(crumbs),
] };
---
<Base
  title="Wildlife Management Plans in Texas | LVG Wildlife Solutions"
  description="A complete wildlife management plan for your property, built from an on-foot assessment. In Texas, prepared to file for wildlife tax exemption with your county."
  path="/wildlife-management-plans"
  ogTitle="Wildlife management plans | LVG Wildlife Solutions"
  ogDescription="What to do for the wildlife on your land, where, and in what order. In Texas, ready to file for wildlife tax exemption."
  current="services"
  ld={ld}
  mcta={{ title: 'Wildlife management plan', line: 'Starts with a site visit', href: '/contact', label: 'Get in touch' }}
>
<PageHead crumbs={crumbs} eyebrow="WILDLIFE MANAGEMENT PLANS" title="A plan for your land, not a template with your name on it" lead="Built from walking your property. It spells out how to manage for the species you care about: which habitat work matters first, what to plant and where, how to handle water and cover, and how to tell whether it is working." />

<section class="topo-ink shift-1 seam">
  <div class="wrap twocol">
    <Figure src="/img/examples/example-map-plan.webp" alt="Example plan map with property boundary, food plots, stands, trail cameras, nest boxes, creek and trails" caption="Every practice in your plan is mapped. Example property, for illustration." w={1800} h={1511} />
    <div>
      <div class="idx"><i></i><s></s><b>WHAT'S IN IT</b></div>
      <h2 class="h2s" style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.3rem)">One package, start to finish</h2>
      <div class="prose"><p>The site visit, the habitat report, the maps, the plan, and help with filing are all part of a management plan. You don't pay for them separately.</p></div>
      <ul class="checks">
        <li><span><b>On-foot assessment</b> of the whole property</span></li>
        <li><span><b>Species goals</b> and the habitat work that serves them</span></li>
        <li><span><b>Food, cover and water</b> prescriptions, mapped and sequenced</span></li>
        <li><span><b>Census and monitoring</b> you can keep up with</span></li>
        <li><span><b>A practice calendar</b> for the year</span></li>
        <li><span><b>Filing help</b> for the Texas wildlife tax exemption</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="dark well topo-gold shift-2">
  <div class="wrap twocol flip">
    <Figure src="/img/examples/example-calendar.webp" alt="Example management calendar showing food plots, brush work, nest boxes, mowing, deer counts, hog control and records by month" caption="Your year, laid out by month. Example for North Texas, for illustration." w={1800} h={1044} />
    <div>
      <div class="idx"><i></i><s></s><b>FOR TEXAS LANDOWNERS</b></div>
      <h2 class="h2s" style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.3rem)">Good management that also counts for your taxes</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Texas offers a wildlife tax exemption for land that already carries an agricultural or timber valuation and is actively managed for native wildlife under a written plan. The state asks for at least three of seven qualifying practices each year, and most good habitat work already falls inside them.</p>
        <p>We prepare your plan on the Texas Parks and Wildlife form and help you file it with your county appraisal district. You sign and file as the owner, and the chief appraiser makes the decision. <a href="/wildlife-tax-valuation">How the wildlife tax exemption works</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="topo-ink shift-3 seam">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="shead">
      <div class="idx"><i></i><s></s><b>AFTER THE PLAN</b></div>
      <h2>Two ways to carry it out</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="who" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr))">
      <div><h3>You do the work</h3><p>Take the plan and carry it out yourself. It tells you what to do, when, and how much, and how to keep the records that back it up.</p></div>
      <div><h3>We get the first year started</h3><p>Have us put the first year's practices on the ground with you: food plots, nest boxes, brush work, and the census. <a href="/habitat-work">Habitat work</a>.</p></div>
      <div><h3>We come back every year</h3><p>A yearly visit, a look back at what changed, and help with the annual report. <a href="/annual-reports">Annual reports and yearly help</a>.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<CtaBand title="Start with a walk of your property" text="Every plan starts with an on-foot assessment. Tell us about your land and we will set up a call." />
</Base>
